Article 10: In accordance with Article 226 of the Civil Procedure Law, under any of the following circumstances, the next higher People's Court may, upon the application of the applicant for enforcement, order the enforcement court to enforce within a time limit or change the enforcement court:
(1) Where, at the time the creditor applies for enforcement, the person subject to execution has property available for enforcement, and the enforcement court has not completed enforcement of such property within more than six months from the date of receipt of the application for enforcement;
(2) Where property available for enforcement of the person subject to execution is discovered during the enforcement process, and the enforcement court has not completed enforcement of such property within more than six months from the date of discovery of the property;
(3) Where, for the enforcement of an obligation of act as determined by a legal instrument, the enforcement court has not taken corresponding enforcement measures according to law within more than six months from the date of receipt of the application for enforcement;
(4) Where there are other circumstances in which enforcement is conditional but has not been enforced within more than six months.
